From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:41:23 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 19/54] Plutonium: windowrequest events, and which element
 drives a window

The app's maximize, unmaximize and minimize requests and its interactive
move and resize (refused while a page shows the window) now reach the page
as a "windowrequest" event (NativeWindowRequestEvent: request, edge). The
app is still answered with its state unchanged; the page decides.

When several elements show one window, one of them drives it: its size is
the window's, and it gets the requests and fullscreen requests. Fullscreen
first, then the one the user last pressed in, then one on screen, then the
last attached. Elements report whether they intersect the viewport and
where their content box is (to tell which one a press landed in); a new
driver sizes the window as it last asked.

Cross-fade: resizes less than 100 ms apart (a drag) show the app live
instead of a stretched old frame over it.

